      "problem": "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\n Find $⟨x(t),y(t)⟩$, if\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2}-2t-3,\\,y(t)={t}^{2}-1.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =0-9+0 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
